"Students analyze how war, displacement, extraction, aid, smuggling, and reconstruction create political-economic systems."}]}, {"id": "3bdcefee-819d-4c8a-b07e-89252620bdf6", "type": "topic", "title": "Neoliberalism, Globalization, and Precarity", "description": "Examines how market-oriented reform and global integration reshape subjectivity, labor, welfare, risk, and political imagination.", "children": [{"id": "7a395e4d-45d6-496e-ac9f-4212ceecdc38", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Neoliberal governance", "children": [{"id": "c5da104b-3073-46ae-9fd8-8cc125102e4d", "type": "concept", "title": "Privatization"}, {"id": "f927f8f9-c8d4-4355-9e93-98ee0e1c6fa6", "type": "concept", "title": "Deregulation"}, {"id": "99a1270b-30c2-4907-90df-16b8172bedb3", "type": "concept", "title": "Entrepreneurial self"}, {"id": "71f5a1e7-a2e3-4580-ae08-dc7d0b77200e", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsibilization"}, {"id": "8295b1cb-c685-472c-89c6-3489ce06da4b", "type": "concept", "title": "Audit culture"}, {"id": "74b3ee0b-1b29-4a6f-b839-e5f64b4facb4", "type": "concept", "title": "Austerity"}], "description": "Students learn how market rationalities reorganize state responsibility, citizenship, and selfhood."}, {"id": "63c9c563-e84e-4f58-8a41-f213c5882b77", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global flows and supply chains", "children": [{"id": "8c5d134e-3b03-4984-b448-ba61ed80b8eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Supply chain"}, {"id": "645f43b8-269d-42cf-89bd-47211a2dae68", "type": "concept", "title": "Outsourcing"}, {"id": "1a8d2b37-62b1-4227-89f2-016203fc6042", "type": "concept", "title": "Logistics"}, {"id": "1e817fc9-bc12-4325-861e-225dd1153289", "type": "concept", "title": "Commodity chain"}, {"id": "cf48efec-a7d3-4363-b44c-4d0dd2bc42bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Export processing zone"}, {"id": "5e617867-d621-4c2e-adda-1c748f821032", "type": "concept", "title": "Global labor"}], "description": "This subtopic connects local livelihoods to transnational production, logistics, finance, and commodity circulation."}, {"id": "4de24717-0276-48b7-b491-c669d6419771", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Precarity and risk", "children": [{"id": "56baae46-d937-4cf6-986f-da910572cd4a", "type": "concept", "title": "Precarity"}, {"id": "71d9430a-1e9d-4e7b-9ec8-be9a49a50f63", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk"}, {"id": "94bb6473-030c-491e-88b2-bd3404bca7a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Informal work"}, {"id": "b3f36cba-bf5f-4ef9-a03e-4cdf3ee59402", "type": "concept", "title": "Gig economy"}, {"id": "f439d514-f414-424c-bded-8a3961709e95", "type": "concept", "title": "Flexibilization"}, {"id": "bd872bc6-b3d2-4c64-a95f-dbc79ec7e378", "type": "concept", "title": "Survival strategy"}], "description": "Students analyze insecurity as a normal condition produced by labor markets, debt, migration, climate, and policy."}]}, {"id": "bc8ecbaf-8b07-455e-a2f9-e03d833fc614", "type": "topic", "title": "Extraction, Environment, and Resource Politics", "description": "Connects political economy to oil, mining, water, forests, fisheries, carbon, infrastructure, toxicity, and environmental justice.", "children": [{"id": "67bef7be-1b61-43cc-9d14-204f3d412eb7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Resource extraction", "children": [{"id": "e50970e1-4e8a-42cf-8bd9-8dee764ba4f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Mining"}, {"id": "63cfd78f-541e-4ac4-b7fe-8808a5c03624", "type": "concept", "title": "Oil"}, {"id": "023f965f-55ec-48de-9afb-75d3e9331eb1", "type": "concept", "title": "Timber"}, {"id": "b842c85c-1607-4666-b246-a5ec337df28a", "type": "concept", "title": "Water"}, {"id": "8315e85e-3acf-46b1-9b5e-d88893049ecd", "type": "concept", "title": "Concession"}, {"id": "a21bc89d-f008-4fe3-96fd-d6c157635114", "type": "concept", "title": "Resource curse"}], "description": "Students examine how extractive projects reorganize land, labor, sovereignty, and social relations."}, {"id": "e6a8c5d5-2dd9-4eb7-a556-3b48b4b0bff8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Infrastructure and logistics", "children": [{"id": "adfa